ace></mstyle><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mover><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">^</mo></mover></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi>s</mi><msqrt><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>j</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace></mstyle><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mtext>SSE</mtext><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> Consequently, the ratio of this one-degree-of-freedom sum of\nsquares to the residual mean square is <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"t_j^2\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msubsup><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D461 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.284em; margin-left: 0;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-spacer style=\"margin-top: 0.18em;\"></mjx-spacer><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D457 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-script></mjx-msubsup></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>.</p>","file":"ch09-sums-of-squares/02-extra-sums.html"}